      {
        "id": "thm-projected-stochastic-gradient-strong-convex-a-s-convergence",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "title": "Projected SGD converges almost surely on a strongly convex objective",
        "statement": "If F=f+ι_C is μ-strongly convex, f has an attained minimizer on nonempty closed convex C, the projected oracle is conditionally unbiased with second moment at most M², and α_k≤1/(2μ), Σα_k=∞, Σα_k²<∞, then x_k converges almost surely to the minimizer.",
